# Patch:     050-name-anonymous-const-assertions
# Phase:     post-extraction
# Target:    extraction/p3_baby_bear.lean
# Hunks:     2
# Cost:      none
# Upstream:  hax bug -- emits `def _`, which is not valid Lean, for Rust's
#            anonymous `const _: () = assert!(..)` items.
# Drop when: hax generates a fresh name for anonymous consts.
#
# `MontyField31::new` carries its Montgomery invariants as anonymous const
# assertions (`const _: () = assert!(..)` in monty-31/src/monty_31.rs). hax
# translates the item but keeps the Rust name, emitting
#
#     def _ : rust_primitives.hax.Tuple0 := ...
#
# `_` is not an identifier in Lean, so the file does not parse. Renamed to
# `const_check_1` and `const_check_2`.
#
# Both hunks are the same bug at two sites, which is why they share one patch:
# fixing it upstream retires both at once. The bodies are untouched -- the
# assertions still elaborate and still carry their `RustM.of_isOk` obligations.
#
--- a/extraction/p3_baby_bear.lean
